  "status": "peer_reviewed",
  "summary": "In a phase 3 trial of 497 patients whose cancer progressed after immunotherapy plus chemotherapy, izalontamab brengitecan beat standard chemotherapy: median progression-free survival was 4.17 vs 1.97 months and median overall survival 9.79 vs 7.20 months. Severe side effects were more common, at 85.1% vs 59.3%. This was an open-label interim analysis at Chinese hospitals only.",
